WEBVTT


00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.048
MY BLIND DATE WITH LIFE


00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.803
BASED ON A TRUE STORY


00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.446
Just follow my lead
and do everything like me.


00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.964
Not bad for a work placement.


00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.129
<i>My name is Saliya Kahawatte.</i>


00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.441
<i>I'd once read this quote</i>


00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.728
<i>by a guy called Buddha.</i>


00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.644
<i>There is no way to happiness.</i>


00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.245
<i>Happiness is the way.</i>


00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.841
<i>I totally agree with him now.</i>


00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.843
<i>But never mind Buddha...</i>


00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.810
<i>the way could've been a lot less rocky.</i>


00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.125
They even let me serve guests


00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.965
although work placements
don't normally do that.


00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.249
The head of personnel said if I want to do
an apprenticeship after A-levels,


00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.642
I'd be more than welcome.
- Wow. that sounds realty great.


00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.490
He's about to burst with pride.


00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.927
He can be proud once he owns the hotel.


00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.606
Says the impoverished Sri Lankan nobility.


00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.890
What's with the origami?
- It's a classic. the bishops mitre.


00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.207
What's wrong?


00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.167
Nothing.


00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.646
The Metamorphosis is a novella
written by Franz Kafka in 1912.


00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.446
Sorry.


00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.725
What's wrong. SaHya?


00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.207
Can't read the handwriting?


00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.366
You're making a fool of yourself.
Sit down.


00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.204
Can you make out anything?


00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.124
No. it's too blurred.


00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.441
Better?


00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.402
No.


00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.728
Sali. can you come with me, please?


00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.083
You can take a seat here.


00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.806
Our examinations show that you suffer
from a hereditary eye disease.


00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.402
Unfortunately. in your case.


00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.685
This has caused a retinal detachment
within a very short period of time.


00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.730
You lost 80 per cent of your sight.


00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.410
Your optic nerve is also damaged


00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.847
and barely able to transmit impulses.


00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.441
We need to operate urgently to preserve
at least a small amount of your eyesight.


00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.486
At least I still have
5 per cent of my eyesight.


00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.529
I've actually been lucky.


00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.164
I'll help you any way I can.


00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.084
I'm not going to a special school.


00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.886
I want to do my A-levels here.
at a normal school.


00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.883
And after that hotel management.


00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:39.484
I won't give up on my original plan
just because of my stupid eyesight.


00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.481
Read.


00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.841
Read it to me.


00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.848
Come on, read it to me.


00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.200
Normal school.


00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.851
You're not normal.


00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.088
Promise me I can stay at my school.


00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.561
<i>Yes. \ promise.</i>


00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.322
Another example for the chain rule:


00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:22.123
y equals e to the power of 4x


00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.685
plus 2.


00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.649
We substitute u for 4x plus 2.


00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.600
Leaving the external function
y equals e to the power of u.


00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.091
Let me know in case I go too fast, Saliya.


00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.322
I will, Mr Ddnges. Thank you.


00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.929
The external derivative remains
y equals e to the power of u


00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.289
<i>while the internal derivative
of 4x plus 2 is 4.</i>


00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.727
I have no idea what he's talking about.


00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.569
This means that y'...


00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.845
equals e to the power of u...


00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.849
...times 4.


00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.522
A second number as a factor...
- A second number as a factor...


00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.330
Don't you want to take a break?


00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.131
You must be tired.


00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.011
I'll have a break after my exams.
Let's carry on.


00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.686
Two fractions.
- Two fractions.


00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:36.484
The sum of arc sine and arc cosine of x


00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.768
is constant...


00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.531
and amounts to...


00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.368
Much as I sympathize. SaHya.
but does it really help, this...


00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.249
murmured repetition?


00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.766
The arc sine of x


00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.447
is 1 divided by the square root of 1
minus x squared,


00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.968
meaning that the sum of arc sine
and arc cosine of x


00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.884
is constant and amounts to...


00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.207
half of pi


00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:11.169
or 1570796327.


00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.803
Well, let's carry on, then.


00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.803
<i>Mum? Sheen?</i>


00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.922
I got my A-levels.


00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.011
A 2.7 average.


00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.570
Congratulations.


00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.326
I probably turned blind
to not have to see you again.


00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.603
<i>I am writing to apply
for an apprentice position at your hotel.</i>


00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.762
<i>I travelled abroad a lot with my parents</i>


00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:10.242
<i>and always wanted to work
in the hotel industry.</i>


00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.005
<i>This summer,</i>


00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.801
<i>I passed my A-levels at the Kan! School
in Neusladt with a 2.7 average.</i>


00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.930
<i>Unfortunately, I was diagnosed
with an eye problem</i>


00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.367
<i>that greatly impairs my vision.</i>


00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.889
<i>Nevertheless, Igained my A-levels
at a normal school.</i>


00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.408
<i>I realize my impairment
makes an apprenticeship a challenge,</i>


00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:32.324
<i>but I'll do everything to make it work.</i>


00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.484
"Unfortunately, your application
has not been successful.


00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.486
We did receive a large number
of applications."


00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:43.241
Disabled people can't be sacked easily.
so they don't get hired.


00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:48.207
A five star hotel?
Mr. Kahawatte, please be realistic.


00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:52.046
With such a severe impairment,
your only option is an apprenticeship


00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.807
as a receptionist or a massage therapist
at a facility for disabled people.


00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:57.530
I can only recommend you


00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.848
stop dreaming.


00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.330
How am I supposed to do that?


00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.249
By acquiring a dreaming impairment?


00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.891
UNFORTUNATELY, I WAS DIAGNOSED
WITH AN EYE PROBLEM...


00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:29.291
You're applying to the Bayerischer Hof
in Munich? And you're not telling them?


00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.488
Yes. H's my only option.


00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.003
I want to lead the life X want to live.


00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:38.084
Without being told,
"you can't do that with your disability."


00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:45.607
<i>In private ownership since 7847,
a Ward- Winning Bayeriscner Hoff</i>


00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.489
<i>with its 340 rooms, including 65 suites,</i>


00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.768
<i>is an institution
amongst the world's luxury hotels.</i>


00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.843
<i>The live events at its nightclub
are legendary. .</i>


00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.002
Eye contact.
That's the most important thing.


00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:08.883
At the same time,
don't forget to keep talking to me.


00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.005
Now then, Mr. Kahawatte.


00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.925
You want to take on
an apprenticeship with us?


00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.603
Yes, I'd like to. That's why I applied.


00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.484
Too low. 15 per cent higher
and you'll meet the eyes.


00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:28.089
Great, that's it.
Now maintain eye contact.


00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.522
Are you prepared to be polite to customers
regardless of how they treat you?


00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.448
I'll cater to their every whim
by the sound of their voice.


00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.126
Great, I'm pleased to welcome you
as a new staff member.


00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:44.562
Thank you.


00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.930
You need to shake my hand.


00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.409
Extend your hand first
for the other to shake it.


00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:53.447
Again.


00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.803
I'm pleased to welcome you...


00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.851
You're meant to shake the hand,
not the breast. - Sorry.


00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.931
Once more: entrance, revolving doors,


00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.686
then 20 steps to the passage
at 12 o'clock.


00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.161
45 degrees right
and 10 steps to the sofas.


00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.766
I stop and look around and wait for
the personnel manager to approach me.


00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:48.763
Perfect. Good luck.


00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:57.331
Whatever happens, we love you.


00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:34.927
Mr. Kahawatte?


00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:39.687
Mr. Fried. head of personnel.
- Thanks for inviting me.


00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.850
Come. I'll show you round while we talk.


00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.286
You just passed your exam.
Why decide against university?


00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:50.086
I decided in favour of
an apprenticeship at your hotel.


00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.250
Excuse me. please.


00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.371
I'm Max Schréder.


00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.170
Our appointment was an hour ago.


00:14:56.320 --> 00:15:00.405
<i>Yes. \ know, but a lorry
crashed into the tram.</i>


00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.689
It derailed,
got stuck in a house entrance,


00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.450
and caused a total road block.


00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:08.080
You may have heard about it on the news.


00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.481
I heard about it. Hello.


00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:18.691
All right, you can accompany us.
We'll start at the very top.


00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:27.206
So after your work placement,
you decided to work in a five star hotel?


00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.966
Much earlier. actually, when I was 14.


00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.645
My father is from Sri Lanka.


00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:36.010
During our summer breaks, we visited his
brother who works at a major hotel there.


00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.521
What fascinated you about it
at the age of 14?


00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.843
I grew up in Neustadt,
which isn't exactly cosmopolitan.


00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.925
But at the hotel, I felt like
the whole world congregated in one place.


00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:51.211
A multitude of languages,
cultures, religions, fashions.


00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:55.088
And they all treated each other
politely and respectfully.


00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:57.607
Just the way it should be in our world.


00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.683
This way, Mr Kahawatte.


00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.564
You OK?
- Thanks.


00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.087
Right. this is one of our suites.


00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.164
Housekeeping would also be one of your...


00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:19.961
modules.


00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.205
If we employ you.


00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.522
Mr Schréder.


00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:29.251
Did you see her? She was hot, wasn't she?


00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:37.203
In the kitchen area, you'll be taught
the basics of high-end cuisine.


00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:42.849
Two chicken supreme,
one fillet of veal, one sea bream.


00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.526
And quick.
- OK.


00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.449
What? Yes. No. Maybe. Piss off!


00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.128
Pretty full-on. isn't it?


00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.884
You always dreamed of working here?


00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.930
Always.
- Since you were 14, like Mr Kahavvatte?


00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.081
Sure, of course.


00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.924
Our head chef, Mr Krohn.


00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.929
Before he joined us,
Mr Krohn worked on a cruise liner,


00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.367
so he runs a tight ship in here.


00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:14.403
Let me finally show you
one of our restaurants.


00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:19.009
We have 15 tables here, virtually
always fully booked, really busy.


00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.841
Mr Kleinschrnidt is in charge of
the restaurant and the adjoining bar.


00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.405
Your third warning.


00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.882
You can finish your apprenticeship
in a youth hostel, don't come back here.


00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.809
He dedicates a lot of time
to the apprentices.


00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:38.247
Do you have a minute? It's about tonight.


00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:42.371
Wait here, I won't be long.
We'll continue with you, Mr Schréder.


00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:51.007
I don't know what it is,
but somethings not quite right with you.


00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:58.250
You said earlier you've always wanted
to work at this hotel.


00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.481
That was a He.


00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.044
If you really wanted this, you wouldn't
be wearing last night's smoky clothes.


00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.247
You wouldn't have been out
drinking all night


00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:11.768
and trying to cover it
with about 20 Fisherman's Friends.


00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:14.771
Shit.


00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:19.603
And you wouldn't have stayed with a girl,
which is probably why you were late.


00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:21.649
How on earth...
- The perfume.


00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:26.850
Unless you like wearing Vera Wang's
"Little Princess" yourself.


00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.006
What are you. the Indian Rain Man?


00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.208
Any old nose can smell that.


00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.921
Maybe Mr Fried hasn't noticed any of this.


00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:42.485
But he'll definitely want to know
why you chose this particular hotel.


00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.166
Having always wanted to work here.


00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:51.320
It was built in 1841.


00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:55.530
Soon it became so prestigious.
even the king visited twice a month


00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.324
as he had no bath tub in his own palace.


00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:04.242
Regularly highest-grossing German hotel,
member of "Leading Hotels of the World".


00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.811
Where were we?


00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:09.487
Mr Schréder. what should your
business card read in 10 years' time?


00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.211
Hotel manager.


00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.443
And why this particular hotel?


00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.809
Or did you only come for an interview
because your dad sent you?


00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:20.449
It's nothing to do with my dad.
It's all about Bayerischer Hof.


00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:24.884
Highest-grossing German hotel.
member of "Leading Hotels of the World".


00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:27.327
Even the king comes here to have a bath.


00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.244
Did come here.


00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:31.721
Follow me.


00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.202
Please wait there. Mr Schréder.


00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.962
Take a seat, Mr Kahavvatte.


00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:50.243
I like what you told me
about the hotel in Sri Lanka.


00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:52.250
An unusual response.


00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.167
You really want this job. don't you?


00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:56.048
I do.


00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.687
I have you down as an honest person.


00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.490
This suits our hotel.


00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:03.971
What's wrong?


00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.850
Mr Kahawatte?


00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.920
Nothing.
- Well, then.


00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.771
I'm pleased to welcome you
as a new staff member.


00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.251
Thank you.


00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.451
Mr Schréder. take a seat.


00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:36.364
They took me.
- What?


00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:39.364
Nobody noticed,
they thought I can see normally.


00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:28.043
Rubbish view. good job you can't see.


00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.001
OK, so there are 28 steps
up to the traffic fights.


00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.730
Take a left there.


00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.247
Then straight
all the way to the tram stop.


00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.767
You can take any tram from there.


00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:02.761
The fifth stop is right outside
the Bayerischer Hof.


00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.490
Let's go.


00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:26.082
This is the last road to cross.


00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:27.847
Mind the step.


00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:35.290
There are about 30 people.


00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.282
You're on your own now.


00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:50.404
You can do this.


00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:55.803
Good luck.
- Thank you.


00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:08.846
Hey. Sali.


00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:11.366
This is it.


00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:13.010
Goodbye to lie-ins.


00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.411
Everyone here?


00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.240
Follow me.


00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:19.921
Let's go.


00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:28.127
Dear apprentices. we have chosen you
out of almost 300 applicants


00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:31.409
because we believe
you have the talent for this career.


00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:34.803
Now it's up to you
to make the best of this talent.


00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:38.203
As of today.
you represent the Bayerischer Hof.


00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:40.442
Its tradition, its reputation.


00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:44.650
And, most of all, the customer service
that always remains our main focus.


00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:47.571
Make sure you are aware
of this responsibility.


00:23:47.720 --> 00:23:51.327
Of course you won't all do
the same stations at the same time.


00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:53.403
Which is why
we're splitting you into groups.


00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:55.085
Mrs Riedinger...


00:23:57.640 --> 00:24:01.167
Hannah Kilmmerle, Saliya Kahavvatte.


00:24:01.320 --> 00:24:02.481
Tim Wasmuth,


00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:04.130
Irina Saizew-Milller.


00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:06.487
Jala Asgari and Max Schréder.


00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:11.042
You'll start your apprenticeship with me,
please follow me.


00:24:33.120 --> 00:24:37.728
I'll now show you
how to fold hospital corners.


00:24:39.040 --> 00:24:41.520
Don't ever let me see this again.
Mr Schréder.


00:24:41.800 --> 00:24:46.886
If I ever catch any of you sitting down.
there will be serious consequences.


00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:52.450
Now watch closely,
you won't learn this at your college.


00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:57.926
Once you're done, you take a step back


00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:01.449
and survey the room
through the eyes of the guest.


00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:04.610
It may look difficult at first,
but in a few weeks


00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:07.650
you'll do the whole room
in less than an hour.


00:25:08.800 --> 00:25:12.122
Now let's try this,
each of you take a room,


00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:15.602
and because it's your first day,
you've got two hours.


00:25:15.880 --> 00:25:17.006
Follow me, please.


00:25:36.880 --> 00:25:38.689
I don't believe it.


00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:42.805
Why doesn't it go away?


00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:48.846
I knew there was something wrong with you.


00:25:53.680 --> 00:25:56.365
What's the matter with you?
- What do you mean?


00:25:57.640 --> 00:25:59.483
Come on, I saw the magnifying glass.


00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:03.209
Retinal detachment.


00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:06.364
I can see 5% of what you're seeing,
which is basically nothing.


00:26:17.800 --> 00:26:19.325
And you didn't tell them?


00:26:19.480 --> 00:26:21.448
Would you have employed me if I had?


00:26:21.600 --> 00:26:22.408
No.


00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:24.643
So please don't tell anyone.


00:26:24.800 --> 00:26:26.529
I can't do that.


00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:30.207
I have to tell Mrs Riedinger.
I cannot cover up fraud.


00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.730
Man, I know you can't...


00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:36.008
You should see your face!


00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:38.689
Of course I won't tell anyone.


00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:40.046
I'm not a dick.


00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:42.169
I'll help you with the mirror.


00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:45.929
What you need...


00:26:47.480 --> 00:26:49.084
is a couple of fresh towels.


00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:53.241
Forget this tiny rag.


00:26:53.400 --> 00:26:57.405
And lots of glass cleaner.


00:26:57.920 --> 00:27:00.685
Apply very liberally.


00:27:01.520 --> 00:27:03.568
And now. towel number one.


00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:07.160
To dry it off. Take this.


00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:12.282
And the second towel is for polishing.


00:27:14.240 --> 00:27:18.211
Once the mirror is done, you toss
the wet towels in the laundry chute.


00:27:18.360 --> 00:27:20.203
Just don't get caught.


00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:21.850
You know all the tricks.


00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:24.731
My dad's in the industry,
he owns a few restaurants.


00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.650
Is that why you're doing this?


00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:28.963
Far from it.


00:27:29.120 --> 00:27:33.489
I failed my Bachelor's twice.
The old man turned off the money supply.


00:27:33.640 --> 00:27:35.483
This is our compromise.


00:27:36.280 --> 00:27:39.409
I want, but can't,
and you can, but don't want to.


00:27:40.080 --> 00:27:43.004
A blind guy and a deaf guy
play dance music. The blind guy asks.


00:27:43.160 --> 00:27:44.571
"Are they already dancing?",


00:27:44.720 --> 00:27:48.042
and the deaf guy replies,
"Have we started playing yet?”


00:27:52.880 --> 00:27:55.451
Now, the junior suites are on the right,


00:27:55.600 --> 00:27:57.807
the senior suites are one floor above.


00:27:57.960 --> 00:27:59.689
Turn left...


00:28:00.880 --> 00:28:01.881
eight steps...


00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:04.247
six steps.


00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:11.404
Sorry, seven steps. I...


00:28:15.640 --> 00:28:17.927
Don't they have hoovers here?


00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.162
And they tell us Germany's modern.


00:28:30.480 --> 00:28:33.006
You also need to learn about cutlery.


00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:36.611
Such as the different cutlery
for starters and mains.


00:28:36.760 --> 00:28:38.842
And you can just remember all this?


00:28:40.600 --> 00:28:43.444
You must be able
to recognise the different glasses.


00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:51.440
Your breakfast.


00:28:51.960 --> 00:28:54.566
Can you put it by the window, please?
- Certainly.


00:29:01.080 --> 00:29:03.082
Good morning.
- Morning.


00:29:10.240 --> 00:29:12.846
Let me know in case
you need anything else.


00:29:29.720 --> 00:29:30.562
I fold.


00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:33.804
So you got the jack?


00:29:33.920 --> 00:29:35.410
Why don't you find out?


00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:42.644
Let's see what you got.


00:29:46.520 --> 00:29:49.171
How can you always tell if I'm bluffing?


00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:22.440
Oh, the room boy.
- I'm sorry.


00:30:22.600 --> 00:30:24.409
Ey. Sali.


00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:26.247
Max?


00:30:26.560 --> 00:30:28.528
Why don't you come in?
There's plenty of room.


00:31:02.120 --> 00:31:03.485
Not bad.


00:31:03.640 --> 00:31:08.487
The entire suite in 110 minutes.
Pretty good for an apprentice.


00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:12.002
I must admit
I had my doubts about you at first.


00:31:12.160 --> 00:31:16.051
But you've really improved a lot, Sallya.
Well clone.


00:31:17.320 --> 00:31:18.401
Thank you.


00:31:48.920 --> 00:31:50.729
Get a beef roast ready.


00:31:53.600 --> 00:31:55.329
A quote by Stevie Wonder:


00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:57.323
I'd rather be blind than black.


00:31:58.120 --> 00:31:59.610
You don't like that one?


00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:08.090
Someone's watching you.
- Who?


00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:10.801
No idea. one of the dishwashers.
Work faster.


00:32:10.960 --> 00:32:14.043
Max, get the dishwasher trolley, hurry up.


00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:23.129
Clean these properly,
or we'll all be in trouble.


00:32:26.360 --> 00:32:28.761
Is there something wrong with your eyes?


00:32:30.640 --> 00:32:32.085
Tell me if you need help.


00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:36.086
Thank you.


00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:37.924
Where are you from?
- Afghanistan.


00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:39.446
What brought you here?


00:32:39.600 --> 00:32:43.002
I fled Kabul.
I was working in a hospital there.


00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:45.083
From surgeon to dishwasher.


00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:49.524
You're not here for small talk, Hamid.
Get back to cleaning those dishes.


00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.287
I don't care. The main thing is
I'm in Germany and got public health care.


00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:57.361
Come on, people. get a move on.


00:33:00.520 --> 00:33:02.568
So?
- He's from Kabul.


00:33:02.720 --> 00:33:04.882
He knows and is going to help me.


00:33:06.760 --> 00:33:09.366
And you, Kawasaki, take out the rubbish.


00:33:09.760 --> 00:33:12.240
What are you waiting for? Move it.


00:33:44.080 --> 00:33:46.845
So it's all about the voice?
- That's it.


00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:50.126
And you can tell
she's the love of your life?


00:33:51.440 --> 00:33:52.487
That's it.


00:33:54.120 --> 00:33:56.248
What if she's super ugly?


00:33:56.400 --> 00:33:57.686
I don't care.


00:33:57.840 --> 00:34:00.241
True, you can't see her anyway.


00:34:00.400 --> 00:34:02.607
With a voice like that,
there's no way she can be ugly.


00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:05.001
Watch out, puddle. Another one!


00:34:05.840 --> 00:34:07.490
Yes!
- Idiot.


00:34:08.240 --> 00:34:10.846
So what now? A blind date?


00:34:11.680 --> 00:34:13.489
That's so lame.


00:34:13.640 --> 00:34:15.165
Three steps coming up.


00:34:15.320 --> 00:34:19.530
Is this Bernd Kégel? This is HR,
we have some brilliant news for you.


00:34:19.760 --> 00:34:20.886
It's regarding...


00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:24.366
Really?


00:34:25.240 --> 00:34:26.446
Me?


00:34:26.760 --> 00:34:30.128
Of course I'll come to your office.
See you shortly.


00:34:33.520 --> 00:34:37.081
Listen here. Kahawatte.
Cover for me, will you?


00:34:37.240 --> 00:34:40.210
There's the organic delivery.
I'm off to see HR.


00:34:40.680 --> 00:34:42.762
I won't be long.
- No worries.


00:34:49.560 --> 00:34:51.130
Morning.


00:34:53.360 --> 00:34:54.441
Where's Bernd?


00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:58.488
He's gone to see HR. I'm covering for him.
- Fine.


00:34:58.640 --> 00:35:00.847
Shall we start?
- Sure.


00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:02.322
Thanks.


00:35:05.880 --> 00:35:08.281
I'm Sali, by the way.
- I'm Laura.


00:35:09.720 --> 00:35:13.008
Are you new here?
- I just started my apprenticeship.


00:35:13.160 --> 00:35:15.242
Freshly delivered. as it were.


00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:18.888
That's an unusual name, "Sali".


00:35:19.040 --> 00:35:24.251
It's short for Saliya. I think it means
"the pious" in Singhalese.


00:35:24.960 --> 00:35:26.121
You're from Sri Lanka?


00:35:27.080 --> 00:35:30.368
My dad is. I'm from provincial Bavaria.


00:35:30.520 --> 00:35:32.284
Neustadt.


00:35:34.160 --> 00:35:35.924
That's nice, too.


00:35:36.080 --> 00:35:37.047
Very.


00:35:39.840 --> 00:35:40.921
So you're pious?


00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:43.681
Yep.


00:35:45.160 --> 00:35:48.403
If I find the guy who
played this trick on me, he'll be sorry.


00:35:49.160 --> 00:35:50.924
The bastard.
- What happened?


00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:54.209
"�Employee of the month."


00:35:54.400 --> 00:35:57.961
Told me to pick up my certificate
from the HR manager.


00:35:58.120 --> 00:36:00.885
And I'm stupid enough to fall for it.


00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:02.764
I'll take over. Thanks, Kahawatte.


00:36:02.920 --> 00:36:07.642
Mr Fried looked at me
as if I was completely insane.


00:36:11.960 --> 00:36:13.610
I got to get back.


00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:15.161
Nice to meet you.


00:36:16.360 --> 00:36:17.930
And you.


00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:20.122
Bye.


00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:32.366
Sali, where the hell have you been?
You're supposed to slice Mortadella.


00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:36.002
You know the slicer. on. off.
adjust the thickness.


00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:38.606
Here's the mortadella. Super easy.


00:36:38.800 --> 00:36:41.804
I want to be able
to see through the slices. Got it?


00:36:52.280 --> 00:36:53.611
Watch out.


00:36:55.720 --> 00:36:57.609
How deep is it?
- Not too bad.


00:36:58.360 --> 00:37:00.010
Hamid, the first aid kit!


00:37:02.760 --> 00:37:04.125
First aid kit!


00:37:08.760 --> 00:37:11.047
When was your last tetanus jab?
- No idea.


00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:14.608
Let's stem the blood flow.


00:37:15.400 --> 00:37:19.200
Sali. come and see me after work today.
OK?


00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:28.444
See you tomorrow.
- Have a nice evening.


00:37:28.640 --> 00:37:29.801
See you.


00:37:30.400 --> 00:37:31.811
Have a nice evening.


00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:43.846
Come over here, please.


00:37:57.480 --> 00:37:59.130
What's wrong with you?


00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:02.365
There are two options.


00:38:02.520 --> 00:38:07.287
Either tell me what's wrong with you,
or don't bother coming back tomorrow.


00:38:09.800 --> 00:38:13.600
I have a problem with the retina.
My eyesight's very poor.


00:38:13.760 --> 00:38:14.682
How poor?


00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:18.602
Five per cent of what you're seeing,
and that's blurred.


00:38:18.760 --> 00:38:20.649
Why are you hiding it?


00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:24.168
Because no-one gave me a chance
being visually impaired.


00:38:27.720 --> 00:38:31.042
I'm sorry. but I can't risk
accidents like that in my kitchen.


00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:40.965
We'll disassemble the food slicer,
I'll explain it,


00:38:41.120 --> 00:38:44.203
you put it back together,
and then you'll master it.


00:38:47.320 --> 00:38:48.924
Thank you.
- Come on.


00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:52.487
Always go for the mains lead first.


00:38:52.720 --> 00:38:55.530
You unplug it like this. Go ahead.


00:38:55.720 --> 00:38:58.929
Never reach into here.
always keep your hand on the outside.


00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:01.606
Always move backwards
across the cutting blade.


00:39:01.760 --> 00:39:02.886
Adjust like this.


00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:04.451
Take it out from the top.


00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:06.364
Now insert the centre hub.


00:39:07.120 --> 00:39:09.327
Line it up. and it's locked on. Good job.


00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:18.130
I think that's enough now.


00:39:26.440 --> 00:39:28.283
So?
- She's pretty.


00:39:28.920 --> 00:39:30.968
But not defined by her prettiness.


00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:36.330
Tell me more.
- She's slender, with nicely defined arms.


00:39:36.960 --> 00:39:39.645
Probably from milking cows
at the organic farm.


00:39:39.800 --> 00:39:42.326
More.
- She's not too tall.


00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.403
She has blond hair, in a plait.


00:39:45.480 --> 00:39:46.367
Perfect.


00:39:46.520 --> 00:39:48.010
She smiles a lot. and...


00:39:51.040 --> 00:39:52.087
She has a boyfriend.


00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:55.846
What?
- I'm sorry.


00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:57.684
Are you sure?


00:39:57.840 --> 00:39:59.842
Pretty sure, they're still snogging.


00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:03.610
Let's drown your sorrows.


00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:22.601
Everyone has several loves of their life,
wouldn't you agree?


00:40:22.760 --> 00:40:23.886
Probably.


00:40:24.040 --> 00:40:27.408
So all you need to do
is move on to the next love of your life.


00:40:27.560 --> 00:40:30.325
It's that easy. is it?
- Yes. it's that easy.


00:40:37.280 --> 00:40:40.682
Maybe ifs one of the two over there.
secretly looking at us.


00:40:40.920 --> 00:40:42.081
Yeah. right.


00:40:42.240 --> 00:40:44.242
<i>I swear. Over at 2 o'clock.</i>


00:40:47.160 --> 00:40:51.006
You know what? I just decided I'll nail
that Indian guy at the bar tonight.


00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:57.929
One of them wants
to nail the "Indian" tonight.


00:40:58.080 --> 00:40:59.286
I knew it. Perfect.


00:40:59.440 --> 00:41:02.330
First, I'm not Indian,
second. I'm still in mourning.


00:41:02.480 --> 00:41:04.767
And she's out of luck
with a voice like that.


00:41:04.920 --> 00:41:06.285
Objection overturned.


00:41:15.320 --> 00:41:18.449
OK, she's coming over.
Green dress. red hair.


00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:21.003
I'd prefer blond hair.


00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:24.209
You want to be blind and picky as well?


00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:27.887
Hello. you beautiful ladies.
I'm Max and this is Sali.


00:41:28.360 --> 00:41:29.930
Hi, I'm Tina.


00:41:37.120 --> 00:41:39.851
Do anything you want to me. will you?


00:41:50.320 --> 00:41:51.401
What's wrong?


00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:52.880
Nothing. it's all good.


00:42:11.800 --> 00:42:14.087
We're all ears. Mr Schrijder.


00:42:14.240 --> 00:42:16.686
Start with the primary fragrances.


00:42:24.840 --> 00:42:25.682
Bear.


00:42:25.840 --> 00:42:28.605
Berry fragrances are found in most wines.


00:42:28.760 --> 00:42:30.842
You need to be more specific.


00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.406
Strawberries?


00:42:40.280 --> 00:42:42.408
Correct. What else?


00:42:51.320 --> 00:42:52.685
We're waiting.


00:42:53.560 --> 00:42:54.846
Blackberries?


00:42:56.480 --> 00:42:58.801
Not bad, Mr Schréder, take a seat.


00:43:01.280 --> 00:43:02.611
How are the scallops?


00:43:02.760 --> 00:43:04.000
Done.
- Get them out.


00:43:04.160 --> 00:43:06.401
How long for this lamb?
- Three minutes. boss.


00:43:06.560 --> 00:43:10.690
Sali. we need to get this out,
one mixed veg. one polenta. How long?


00:43:10.840 --> 00:43:11.762
Nearly done.


00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:14.048
Three minutes for the polenta. Taste it.


00:43:14.560 --> 00:43:17.245
Come on, Max, step on it,
the salmon needs to go in the oven.


00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:23.405
Jan is gonna show you how to stuff it.
Let's hope you scaled it properly.


00:43:23.640 --> 00:43:25.085
Here we go. Tim.


00:43:25.920 --> 00:43:28.685
Jala. Hannah.


00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:32.002
Irina. Well done.


00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:34.528
Your next module is reception, isn't it?


00:43:34.680 --> 00:43:36.091
I'll stick to the dishes.


00:43:37.440 --> 00:43:38.521
Good luck.


00:43:39.080 --> 00:43:39.842
Thank you.


00:43:41.280 --> 00:43:43.282
Thanks for everything.


00:44:10.360 --> 00:44:11.247
Thanks.


00:45:00.560 --> 00:45:02.324
Leave it.


00:45:05.880 --> 00:45:07.484
OK. Kleinschrnidt is gone.


00:45:08.360 --> 00:45:10.966
Did your son get his university place?
- You remembered that?


00:45:11.480 --> 00:45:12.481
Yes. he did.


00:45:12.640 --> 00:45:14.688
Tell him congratulations.
- We will.


00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:17.407
Room 291. Enjoy your stay.


00:45:23.240 --> 00:45:25.242
Teacher's pet.


00:45:25.520 --> 00:45:27.284
You better believe it.


00:45:33.200 --> 00:45:36.363
Four tables on each side.
each of them three steps apart.


00:45:36.560 --> 00:45:38.608
The bar's eleven steps long
and three steps wide.


00:45:38.960 --> 00:45:40.450
11 steps.


00:45:40.600 --> 00:45:42.682
This is your final module.


00:45:42.840 --> 00:45:44.490
But it'll be the hardest.


00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:47.163
Great service makes a hotel.


00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:50.164
You'll start before
the first guest arrives


00:45:50.320 --> 00:45:52.721
and you'll leave
long after the last one has left.


00:45:52.920 --> 00:45:54.843
You'll be there whenever needed,


00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:59.130
silent. unobtrusive and,
most importantly, with a smile.


00:46:00.080 --> 00:46:05.166
Don't forget. if you smile from the heart,
the customer knows you love your job.


00:46:05.320 --> 00:46:10.804
I will not tolerate sloppiness,
tardiness, laziness,


00:46:10.960 --> 00:46:14.089
or anything else that might
tarnish the hotel's reputation.


00:46:14.240 --> 00:46:18.040
And now the gents fetch the drinks
while the ladies stock up.


00:46:32.880 --> 00:46:34.530
Yummy, yummy. yummy-


00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:50.004
Can you help me out, Sali?


00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:53.050
The authorities again?
- Yes. another letter.


00:46:53.200 --> 00:46:54.964
Salim aleikum.
- Greetings.


00:46:55.280 --> 00:46:58.409
Listen. "Dear Mr Hamid Mousafa.


00:46:58.560 --> 00:47:00.642
Referring to our letter regarding


00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:03.087
your appeal of our rejection
of your request


00:47:03.440 --> 00:47:06.364
to alter your temporary...


00:47:06.760 --> 00:47:09.331
your temporary employment contract..."


00:47:18.320 --> 00:47:20.527
Laura waived at you.
You didn't waive back.


00:47:20.720 --> 00:47:22.643
So I waived for you.


00:47:23.200 --> 00:47:25.168
She's gone.
- Where did she go?


00:47:25.800 --> 00:47:28.565
She went outside.
- I'll be right back.


00:47:41.040 --> 00:47:43.361
Hamid said you waived at me.


00:47:43.520 --> 00:47:44.931
I'm sorry. I didn't see it.


00:47:47.200 --> 00:47:50.170
What do you do for Hamid?
- I help him with official letters.


00:47:50.320 --> 00:47:52.926
He's actually a doctor
and wants to be a paramedic.


00:47:53.880 --> 00:47:56.724
But his passport only allows him
to work here, washing dishes.


00:47:57.040 --> 00:47:58.371
It's complicated.


00:47:58.560 --> 00:47:59.925
How are you?


00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:02.208
Not bad. And yourself?


00:48:02.360 --> 00:48:03.521
I'm fine.


00:48:03.680 --> 00:48:05.603
How's it going with... Mina?


00:48:07.400 --> 00:48:09.164
You're together, aren't you?


00:48:09.320 --> 00:48:11.084
No. definitely not.


00:48:11.720 --> 00:48:14.610
We're not together. by mutual consent.


00:48:16.240 --> 00:48:20.564
What about you?
How's it going with... your colleague?


00:48:20.720 --> 00:48:22.370
We split up.


00:48:22.520 --> 00:48:24.727
Not by mutual consent.


00:48:25.960 --> 00:48:28.850
Sorry to hear that.
- Don't be. He was a dick.


00:48:30.200 --> 00:48:32.680
This might be shooting
from the hip, but...


00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:35.210
would you go out for dinner with me?


00:48:35.360 --> 00:48:37.328
What gave you that idea?


00:48:39.280 --> 00:48:41.009
Only joking.


00:48:42.680 --> 00:48:44.523
Tomorrow? You choose the restaurant?


00:48:46.520 --> 00:48:49.444
I can't do tomorrow. How about Saturday?


00:48:50.680 --> 00:48:52.409
Sure. Great.


00:48:52.760 --> 00:48:54.046
See you then.


00:48:58.720 --> 00:49:03.328
You carefully put the ice
into a tall glass using bar tongues.


00:49:03.560 --> 00:49:04.971
Just a few ice cubes.


00:49:05.960 --> 00:49:08.884
Now you take the measuring cone.
called a jigger.


00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:11.930
And measure 150i each of vodka,


00:49:13.360 --> 00:49:14.600
white rum.


00:49:14.840 --> 00:49:16.763
Tequila. gin,


00:49:17.480 --> 00:49:19.164
2cl of Cointreau,


00:49:19.480 --> 00:49:21.369
and finally a dash of lemon juice.


00:49:22.160 --> 00:49:24.288
Into the cooled shaker,
put the lid on,


00:49:24.960 --> 00:49:28.442
shake vigorously
with a few determined movements.


00:49:30.360 --> 00:49:32.169
Insert strainer. and pour.


00:49:33.320 --> 00:49:35.209
Top up the glass with coke.


00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:37.926
Cut some lemon zest,


00:49:38.080 --> 00:49:39.286
roll it,


00:49:40.720 --> 00:49:42.324
one squirt.


00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:44.960
Two slices of lemon for decoration.


00:49:45.160 --> 00:49:46.605
Straw.


00:49:48.120 --> 00:49:49.485
Stirrer.


00:49:49.680 --> 00:49:50.806
And then...


00:49:52.320 --> 00:49:54.527
serve the Long Island Ice Tea
to the guest.


00:49:56.720 --> 00:49:59.166
Then you swipe the card at the register.


00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.843
You select the table.


00:50:02.040 --> 00:50:04.042
The numbers are on this list.


00:50:04.200 --> 00:50:07.283
And then print and file the receipt.


00:50:07.960 --> 00:50:09.450
Any questions?


00:50:13.600 --> 00:50:16.888
Voila. my old man's restaurant.


00:50:20.040 --> 00:50:21.929
Feel free to look around.


00:50:23.160 --> 00:50:26.767
8962... Campari and soda.


00:50:29.760 --> 00:50:32.764
Classic... rnojito.


00:50:34.520 --> 00:50:36.921
Cuba... libre.


00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:38.326
How many d?


00:50:38.640 --> 00:50:40.847
4cl of white rum.


00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:42.445
Cuban rum.


00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:45.367
12cl of coke and 2 limes.


00:50:48.760 --> 00:50:50.728
One, two, three...
- Stop!


00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:52.881
Too much.


00:50:57.560 --> 00:50:58.322
Again.


00:51:03.720 --> 00:51:04.846
Almost.


00:51:11.200 --> 00:51:13.282
Shouldn't we use water instead?


00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:17.525
Rubbish. Water has a totally different
density to vodka. Try again.


00:51:23.400 --> 00:51:24.811
Perfect.


00:51:27.200 --> 00:51:28.690
Once more for practice.


00:51:32.680 --> 00:51:34.125
Very good.


00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:36.411
Fantastic.


00:51:37.840 --> 00:51:39.729
I'm proud of you. mum.


00:51:40.480 --> 00:51:42.482
Cheers to that.


00:52:29.040 --> 00:52:31.566
I think I'll take Laura here for dinner.


00:52:36.560 --> 00:52:39.962
Take the menu and wine list with you
and learn them by heart.


00:52:40.120 --> 00:52:41.963
Thanks.
- Are you picking her up?


00:52:42.680 --> 00:52:45.047
Too complicated and too risky.


00:52:46.680 --> 00:52:48.091
I'll suggest we meet here.


00:52:49.320 --> 00:52:52.210
Wouldn't it be easier
if you told her the truth?


00:52:52.360 --> 00:52:56.968
If I did that. it would be the only topic.
I don't want that on a first date.


00:52:57.120 --> 00:53:01.125
I might as well just forget it.
- So when are you going to tell her?


00:53:01.320 --> 00:53:04.085
No idea. But not on our first date.


00:53:07.520 --> 00:53:11.809
Don't give me that quizzical look.
- I'm looking at a girl in the street.


00:53:12.440 --> 00:53:13.805
No. you're not.
- Yes. I am.


00:53:15.760 --> 00:53:17.125
You know what?


00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:21.402
You should order the gnocchi.
you can spoon them without looking.


00:54:13.000 --> 00:54:15.367
Not bad, Schréder, a well-pulled Pilsener.


00:54:15.520 --> 00:54:17.249
I'm an expert on spirits.


00:54:17.400 --> 00:54:20.244
I thought as much,
going by how you look in the mornings.


00:54:20.400 --> 00:54:23.244
Beer isn't a spirit, by the way.
Thinner slices.


00:54:30.240 --> 00:54:32.368
One Long Island Ice Tea.


00:54:35.360 --> 00:54:36.600
Enjoy.


00:54:55.640 --> 00:54:56.687
Not bad, Kahavvatte.


00:54:56.840 --> 00:54:59.446
But even a blind man
may perchance hit the mark.


00:55:34.360 --> 00:55:37.569
Have you been waiting long?
- I only just arrived myself.


00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:42.121
Nice place.


00:55:44.640 --> 00:55:46.165
Can you recommend anything?


00:55:46.320 --> 00:55:48.004
The risottos are great.


00:55:48.440 --> 00:55:50.010
Page two under "Primi".


00:55:54.920 --> 00:55:56.365
Great, I'll go for that.


00:55:58.440 --> 00:56:00.522
Here we have the risotto with asparagus.


00:56:00.680 --> 00:56:01.886
Thank you.


00:56:02.400 --> 00:56:05.006
And the gnocchi.
- Thanks.


00:56:05.160 --> 00:56:06.321
Enjoy your meal.


00:56:07.640 --> 00:56:08.687
Enjoy.


00:56:08.880 --> 00:56:09.642
You too.


00:56:15.800 --> 00:56:17.768
How long have you been at the farm?


00:56:17.920 --> 00:56:19.251
About three years.


00:56:19.400 --> 00:56:20.811
I was living in the city before.


00:56:20.960 --> 00:56:23.247
Do you like it there?
Are your bosses nice?


00:56:23.400 --> 00:56:25.050
Very nice. They're my parents.


00:56:26.320 --> 00:56:29.210
It's your parents' farm?
- Yes. I grew up there.


00:56:29.920 --> 00:56:31.649
So you went back there?


00:56:32.240 --> 00:56:37.167
Yes. it wasn't the way I planned it.
living with my parents again,


00:56:37.360 --> 00:56:39.601
but as a mum
I didn't want to cut myself off,


00:56:39.760 --> 00:56:41.842
so this was the best solution.


00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:43.001
You have a child?


00:56:43.760 --> 00:56:45.046
Oskar. He's five.


00:56:47.320 --> 00:56:52.087
Yes. "wow". that's exactly
what my parents said when they found out.


00:56:52.240 --> 00:56:54.527
And they're looking after him right now?


00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:58.810
Yes. I always thought it was a cliche,
but you go out very selectively.


00:57:59.880 --> 00:58:03.726
It's not exactly a new concept.
but if I'm an expert in one area,


00:58:03.880 --> 00:58:07.123
it's where the best meat
and the best vegetables come from.


00:58:07.520 --> 00:58:10.967
It would have to be unique, though.
not just another beef place.


00:58:11.960 --> 00:58:15.123
Sinhalese cuisine.
- Sure. Because I'm the total expert.


00:58:15.320 --> 00:58:16.367
But I am.


00:58:18.640 --> 00:58:19.801
Sounds good.


00:58:20.640 --> 00:58:24.770
I'm taking Oskar to the river on Sunday,
would you like to join us?


00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:28.647
You don't have to, only if you fancy it.


00:58:28.800 --> 00:58:30.609
I do, of course I fancy it.


00:58:30.800 --> 00:58:31.961
See you Sunday.


00:58:32.200 --> 00:58:33.281
See you Sunday.


00:59:39.920 --> 00:59:41.160
Have you decided?


00:59:42.800 --> 00:59:44.211
This one. please.


00:59:47.960 --> 00:59:49.246
Right away. sir.


00:59:49.720 --> 00:59:52.087
This is it, The Arrogant Frog.


00:59:54.200 --> 00:59:55.440
Excuse me. please.


00:59:57.360 --> 00:59:58.725
Jameson. Gold Reserve.


01:00:01.920 --> 01:00:03.684
How did it go with Laura?
- Great.


01:00:04.600 --> 01:00:06.807
So? Did you tell her?


01:00:07.960 --> 01:00:08.768
No.


01:00:12.520 --> 01:00:14.761
Where were we?
The Arrogant Frog.


01:00:15.280 --> 01:00:17.760
The eponymous amphibian is almost extinct,


01:00:17.920 --> 01:00:23.006
however, at this vineyard,
it still enjoys rude health and virility.


01:00:23.480 --> 01:00:26.006
In that case,
I'll try a glass of the frog wine.


01:00:26.160 --> 01:00:27.241
With pleasure.


01:00:31.120 --> 01:00:32.087
Right away.


01:00:32.240 --> 01:00:33.890
Yes. VII be right with you.


01:01:01.400 --> 01:01:02.925
I'm off to bed.


01:01:03.120 --> 01:01:04.201
Goodnight.


01:01:14.960 --> 01:01:16.803
So... are you finished?


01:01:17.320 --> 01:01:18.287
Yes.


01:01:18.760 --> 01:01:20.171
Step aside.


01:01:33.880 --> 01:01:37.168
You'll now wash up and polish
all the glasses again,


01:01:37.320 --> 01:01:41.120
and if they still show stains,
you'll wash up and polish them yet again.


01:01:41.800 --> 01:01:43.802
Do you understand me. Kahawatte?


01:01:43.960 --> 01:01:45.769
Yes.
- Good.


01:02:10.280 --> 01:02:12.123
Are you done?
- Nearly.


01:02:18.760 --> 01:02:22.526
You stay until you learned
how to polish glasses. Go ahead.


01:02:22.680 --> 01:02:24.284
Do them again.


01:02:39.560 --> 01:02:41.289
Give it to me.


01:02:43.360 --> 01:02:45.283
No, still not clean, Kahawatte.


01:02:45.600 --> 01:02:46.726
Do it again.


01:02:59.920 --> 01:03:02.651
No. you tell me if it's clean.


01:03:08.800 --> 01:03:11.007
Is this glass clean or not?


01:03:19.560 --> 01:03:22.086
Surely you can see
if a glass is dean or not?


01:03:23.520 --> 01:03:25.443
I don't know.
- What?


01:03:25.680 --> 01:03:28.570
I don't know. I'm tired. We had enough.


01:03:30.800 --> 01:03:35.328
We'll carry on until you know.
Once again, wash up and polish.


01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:39.964
One other thing, Kahawatte,
your manner just now.


01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:43.010
Do you lose your temper
with the guests as well?


01:03:44.920 --> 01:03:47.730
This is your first warning.
Three and you're out.


01:04:37.400 --> 01:04:40.051
This is a nice spot, isn't it?
- Very nice.


01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:45.207
Come on, Sali, let's play football.


01:04:45.360 --> 01:04:47.169
Is that OK?
- Yeah, sure.


01:04:51.520 --> 01:04:53.807
There's the goal.
- Over there? OK.


01:04:53.960 --> 01:04:55.962
Where the sticks are.


01:04:56.120 --> 01:04:58.487
The sticks... OK.


01:05:22.760 --> 01:05:24.762
I'll have a little rest.


01:05:28.560 --> 01:05:30.483
Oskar is full of energy.


01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:57.245
What are you doing?


01:05:58.800 --> 01:06:00.848
I'm sorry. I thought you were asleep.


01:06:02.360 --> 01:06:05.284
This is what you do to sleeping women?
- No, I...


01:06:05.440 --> 01:06:07.522
Sali. come and play with us.


01:06:08.400 --> 01:06:10.050
Your son needs me.


01:06:39.480 --> 01:06:40.720
I'll ask him, sweetie.


01:06:44.240 --> 01:06:46.322
Oskar wants to ask you something.


01:06:57.000 --> 01:06:58.570
Hey. Oskar.


01:06:59.600 --> 01:07:00.806
What's up?


01:07:00.960 --> 01:07:02.371
Are you an alien?


01:07:03.560 --> 01:07:05.403
Why do you think that?


01:07:05.560 --> 01:07:09.724
Because they don't play football
on your planet.


01:07:12.520 --> 01:07:14.090
Don't worry.


01:07:14.800 --> 01:07:17.246
I'm not an alien.
- OK.


01:07:17.400 --> 01:07:22.008
But if you are, will you promise
not to eat Mummy and me?


01:07:23.560 --> 01:07:26.006
I'll even make sure no-one else eats you.


01:07:26.400 --> 01:07:28.607
OK. I'll go to sleep, then.


01:07:39.440 --> 01:07:41.886
Seems like a match made in heaven.


01:07:42.040 --> 01:07:45.249
Are you staying for a drink?
- I'd love to.


01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:12.763
What happened to Oskar's dad?


01:08:12.920 --> 01:08:14.251
We lost touch.


01:08:15.560 --> 01:08:20.964
At first he was all for it, but once Oskar
was born, he wanted his old life back.


01:08:21.120 --> 01:08:24.169
He moved to Berlin. Doesn't call anymore.
- Unbelievable.


01:08:24.320 --> 01:08:26.288
It's easier without him.


01:08:26.440 --> 01:08:29.887
Plus, I don't have to deal
with his permanent lies anymore.


01:08:31.640 --> 01:08:32.527
What is it?


01:08:35.160 --> 01:08:36.082
What's wrong?


01:08:39.280 --> 01:08:40.930
Everything's fine.


01:08:42.240 --> 01:08:44.208
Goodnight.
- Goodnight.


01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:49.161
Safe journey home.


01:09:26.680 --> 01:09:27.727
Now the main course.


01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:34.085
The same basic principle applies:
never reach over a guest's plate.


01:09:35.200 --> 01:09:37.487
Remember to always adhere to
the direction of service.


01:09:46.880 --> 01:09:48.689
Your first day at the restaurant


01:09:48.840 --> 01:09:50.490
and you're late?


01:09:51.000 --> 01:09:53.480
I'm so sorry,
I didn't hear the alarm clock.


01:09:59.000 --> 01:10:01.002
This is your second warning.


01:10:01.160 --> 01:10:03.640
You'll receive this one in writing.


01:10:04.640 --> 01:10:07.371
You are one step away from the red line.


01:10:08.400 --> 01:10:09.845
What's this?


01:10:18.000 --> 01:10:20.002
What's with your cravat. Kahawatte?


01:10:23.240 --> 01:10:25.766
Shall we call you "Crahavatte"
from now on?


01:10:25.920 --> 01:10:27.763
Would that be easier?


01:10:27.920 --> 01:10:30.127
Only for you.
- What did you say?


01:10:32.360 --> 01:10:34.010
It would be easier for you.


01:10:34.760 --> 01:10:37.843
I hope you don't have a problem
with heartfelt dislike.


01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:40.651
No problem, that's just like at home.


01:10:40.800 --> 01:10:43.326
Well, we want you to feel
very much at home here.


01:10:43.480 --> 01:10:46.962
Now then, on to our next exercise,
setting a table.


01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:52.809
3 MISSED CALLS


01:10:57.120 --> 01:11:00.010
He took all the jewellery
and any valuables.


01:11:00.640 --> 01:11:03.166
He also cleared out all the bank accounts.


01:11:04.400 --> 01:11:08.644
Last week. he married
another woman in Sri Lanka.


01:11:09.840 --> 01:11:13.242
He had his life insurance
transferred over to her.


01:11:13.400 --> 01:11:18.406
He somehow managed to have his marriage
to me annulled over there.


01:11:19.280 --> 01:11:22.682
To pay the rates on the house,
Mum urgently needs to find a job.


01:11:22.840 --> 01:11:24.285
Which won't be easy.


01:11:24.840 --> 01:11:28.128
Your dad never wanted me to have a job.
- I know.


01:11:28.320 --> 01:11:29.685
Is there anything I can do?


01:11:29.840 --> 01:11:33.686
Pass your exams.
It'll be one less thing to worry about.


01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:37.161
I'm sorry.


01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:45.971
I can transfer 200 euros a month to Mum.
And I'M find a second job.


01:11:46.120 --> 01:11:47.724
Hamid works part-time at a bakery.


01:11:48.720 --> 01:11:50.688
How is this supposed to work?


01:11:50.840 --> 01:11:52.649
You're already overworked.


01:11:53.880 --> 01:11:55.450
I can do this.


01:11:56.240 --> 01:11:58.720
It'll only be until Mum has found a job.


01:11:59.480 --> 01:12:00.925
But don't tell her, OK?


01:12:33.760 --> 01:12:34.807
Wrong Way-


01:12:36.720 --> 01:12:39.724
At this pace,
you'll never pass the final exam.


01:12:43.080 --> 01:12:44.570
Not too high, Oskar!


01:12:46.800 --> 01:12:48.768
Look how high I am!


01:13:42.160 --> 01:13:45.562
Catch me!
- No. I'm not good at that!


01:13:51.920 --> 01:13:53.126
One...
- No!


01:13:53.280 --> 01:13:55.362
Two...
- Don't!


01:13:59.720 --> 01:14:00.403
Three!


01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:05.684
That was cool! Again!


01:14:15.880 --> 01:14:20.488
You're a tiny step from tearing down the
house of cards you so carefully set up.


01:14:48.840 --> 01:14:51.889
Thank you so much.
I need to do my dad's deliveries.


01:14:52.360 --> 01:14:53.771
It'll only take an hour.


01:14:53.920 --> 01:14:55.046
No problem at all.


01:14:55.200 --> 01:14:57.771
Oskar prefers you playing with him anyway.


01:14:58.880 --> 01:15:00.689
Where is he?
- In the sand pit.


01:15:00.880 --> 01:15:02.450
He's building your UFO.


01:15:03.840 --> 01:15:05.763
See you in a bit. I'll be quick.


01:15:06.240 --> 01:15:07.366
Bye. Oskar.


01:15:14.840 --> 01:15:17.002
Hello. alien.


01:15:17.400 --> 01:15:18.845
Hello.


01:15:40.240 --> 01:15:41.924
Who on earth is this now?


01:15:47.160 --> 01:15:48.241
Max, what's up?


01:15:48.520 --> 01:15:52.525
Kleinschmidt will be here any minute.
If you're not here that's you finished.


01:15:54.440 --> 01:15:55.726
I totally forgot.


01:15:56.040 --> 01:15:59.647
I'm looking after Oskar.
I'll come as quickly as I can.


01:15:59.800 --> 01:16:01.689
Laura should be back any minute.


01:16:01.880 --> 01:16:03.211
See you shortly.


01:16:21.960 --> 01:16:25.009
Laura, listen. there's this
wedding reception at the hotel,


01:16:25.160 --> 01:16:27.162
I totally forgot I'm on the service list.


01:16:28.320 --> 01:16:30.687
I should have been there ages ago.


01:16:30.840 --> 01:16:35.448
You're nearly back anyway? That's great.
See you in a minute. Bye.


01:16:57.720 --> 01:17:00.644
Oskar. if this is a game
you must stop it now.


01:17:07.440 --> 01:17:08.805
This is not funny!


01:17:09.040 --> 01:17:10.166
Why is he shouting?


01:17:27.040 --> 01:17:28.280
What's wrong?


01:17:28.440 --> 01:17:30.807
I lost Oskar.
I was only on the phone for a moment.


01:17:31.240 --> 01:17:33.288
Oskar's gone.
- Since when?


01:17:33.600 --> 01:17:35.841
A few minutes. He was here a moment ago.


01:17:40.240 --> 01:17:41.685
Come on, Sali, help me look.


01:17:46.120 --> 01:17:47.360
What is it?


01:17:47.720 --> 01:17:49.609
<i>I can't help you look. \ can't see.</i>


01:17:58.680 --> 01:18:01.570
Have you seen
a five year old boy with a blue hat?


01:18:11.760 --> 01:18:13.569
You mustn't run away like that.


01:18:14.920 --> 01:18:18.845
Never just walk off.
You must always tell me where you go.


01:18:30.440 --> 01:18:32.488
What do you mean, you can't see?


01:18:34.320 --> 01:18:36.084
I have an eye defect.


01:18:37.520 --> 01:18:40.729
I can see only five per cent
of what you're seeing.


01:18:41.560 --> 01:18:45.087
You look after my child
without telling me you can't see?


01:19:09.160 --> 01:19:12.209
Kleinschmidfs here.
Turn up soon or you're finished.


01:19:14.080 --> 01:19:15.570
I'll be there in five minutes.


01:19:17.960 --> 01:19:21.521
You're not supposed to use your phone.
- Won't happen again.


01:19:28.240 --> 01:19:31.244
You have table three.
25 steps at 2 o'clock.


01:19:31.400 --> 01:19:33.926
I don't think Kleinschmidt
noticed you're late.


01:19:34.680 --> 01:19:36.569
Are you all right?
- Yes.


01:19:36.920 --> 01:19:38.251
Gotta get back.


01:19:45.600 --> 01:19:49.321
There you are. Table three
are waiting for their champagne.


01:20:16.680 --> 01:20:18.967
Careful. Don't cut yourself.


01:20:34.480 --> 01:20:37.006
This is pointless. You're not with it.


01:20:37.160 --> 01:20:39.208
If I leave, that's it.


01:20:39.760 --> 01:20:43.526
Man, you're totally out of it.
You can't work like this.


01:20:44.480 --> 01:20:45.242
Let go.


01:20:45.520 --> 01:20:49.809
Sali, I'm your friend
but you're turning into a complete idiot.


01:20:50.120 --> 01:20:52.248
If you go back in, I can't help you.


01:20:56.480 --> 01:20:58.528
You're on your own. then.


01:21:15.920 --> 01:21:19.402
Idiot! What are you doing?
Are you blind?


01:21:19.560 --> 01:21:21.528
Yes, damn it. I am blind.


01:21:21.680 --> 01:21:22.647
What?


01:21:23.480 --> 01:21:26.086
And you didn't notice all this time.


01:21:26.240 --> 01:21:28.527
Get out of here. Now. Out.


01:22:31.400 --> 01:22:34.961
Quit the drugs, Sali. Non-functioning eyes
and brain is too much.


01:22:35.080 --> 01:22:36.570
Mind your own business.


01:23:03.680 --> 01:23:05.045
You had enough.


01:23:17.960 --> 01:23:19.530
Watch out!


01:23:33.400 --> 01:23:35.129
I'll call an ambulance.
- You OK?


01:23:35.280 --> 01:23:38.090
What's your name?
Can you tell me your name?


01:23:38.240 --> 01:23:40.846
Can you hear me? Can you see me?


01:24:16.520 --> 01:24:19.330
Man, I can't let you
out of my eyes for even a minute.


01:24:27.520 --> 01:24:30.842
I'm sorry about the way I behaved.
I've really been a dick.


01:24:31.880 --> 01:24:33.769
You've really been a dick.


01:24:34.680 --> 01:24:37.763
For not telling me that you have


01:24:37.920 --> 01:24:40.571
such an unbelievably good-looking sister.


01:24:44.840 --> 01:24:46.729
Protective instinct.


01:24:49.480 --> 01:24:52.529
Come with me to Neustadt.
Mum would be so happy.


01:24:52.920 --> 01:24:55.605
She found a job at an insurance company.


01:24:55.800 --> 01:24:57.802
It means we can keep the house.


01:25:06.160 --> 01:25:08.640
I can't live against my disability.


01:25:08.800 --> 01:25:10.689
It won't work. I know that now.


01:25:12.520 --> 01:25:17.560
If the hotels don't want me, I'll find
an employer for visually impaired people.


01:25:20.280 --> 01:25:21.930
But here.


01:25:22.880 --> 01:25:24.564
In Munich.


01:25:30.360 --> 01:25:32.249
Come. this way, please.


01:25:32.880 --> 01:25:37.010
Between 30 and 40 per cent of our
operators are blind or visually impaired


01:25:37.160 --> 01:25:40.243
which makes us Munich's largest
equality employer.


01:25:41.080 --> 01:25:45.210
We offer special schooling and training
courses to our disabled staff.


01:25:45.360 --> 01:25:48.091
You'll be able to benefit from them, too.


01:26:02.360 --> 01:26:03.122
So?


01:26:03.960 --> 01:26:05.849
I can't work there. No Way.


01:26:06.520 --> 01:26:09.285
I thought so. What now?


01:26:09.680 --> 01:26:11.489
Train to become a massage therapist?


01:26:14.000 --> 01:26:16.924
There's one thing
I've always wanted to do with you.


01:26:17.200 --> 01:26:19.328
And now's the perfect time for it.


01:26:35.120 --> 01:26:36.690
It's not steep at all.


01:26:37.640 --> 01:26:40.405
Plus, you're experienced
at falling over now.


01:26:50.280 --> 01:26:52.169
Now right, OK? Right!


01:27:07.320 --> 01:27:09.049
Straight on.


01:27:10.800 --> 01:27:12.564
Stay with me.


01:27:19.000 --> 01:27:20.365
Stay with me.


01:27:22.080 --> 01:27:22.922
Brake!


01:27:24.720 --> 01:27:26.802
Now keep left.


01:27:31.240 --> 01:27:32.241
Straight.


01:27:33.840 --> 01:27:34.807
Left.


01:27:37.720 --> 01:27:39.324
Obstacle!


01:27:39.480 --> 01:27:40.322
Obstacle?


01:27:40.440 --> 01:27:41.407
Brake!


01:27:54.360 --> 01:27:55.486
I'm fine!


01:27:57.840 --> 01:28:00.525
It's not his fault. He's blind as a bat.


01:28:01.520 --> 01:28:02.806
Let's go.


01:28:10.800 --> 01:28:12.040
Brake!


01:28:33.320 --> 01:28:34.685
When's the exam?


01:28:58.840 --> 01:29:00.080
What are you doing here?


01:29:00.560 --> 01:29:02.403
I've come to apologise.


01:29:02.840 --> 01:29:05.207
To you, Mr Kleinschmidt, to you, Mr Fried,


01:29:05.360 --> 01:29:10.321
and to the others for lying to you
throughout the whole training.


01:29:11.840 --> 01:29:13.330
I'm truly sorry.


01:29:15.920 --> 01:29:18.890
And spoiling that couple's wedding was...


01:29:19.080 --> 01:29:20.047
inexcusable.


01:29:21.480 --> 01:29:22.641
What do you want?


01:29:24.920 --> 01:29:26.763
Please let me take the exam.


01:29:32.520 --> 01:29:36.764
Before I applied here. people told me


01:29:36.920 --> 01:29:42.051
to be realistic, to stop dreaming
and forget about an apprenticeship.


01:29:42.440 --> 01:29:47.480
Maybe I achieved more by lying
than I would have being honest.


01:29:47.680 --> 01:29:50.411
But giving in wasn't an option for me.


01:29:51.440 --> 01:29:53.727
So from now on. I'll stand by who I am.


01:29:54.880 --> 01:29:58.680
A guy who can't do without his friends
because he's crap at seeing.


01:30:01.360 --> 01:30:04.921
But I won't give up dreaming. Never.


01:30:06.720 --> 01:30:09.166
Let me prove to you that I can do it.


01:30:09.920 --> 01:30:11.684
Please give me this chance.


01:30:15.840 --> 01:30:17.524
Please, Mr Kleinschmidt.


01:30:18.080 --> 01:30:21.641
You're convinced I'll fail anyway.
the way I set tables.


01:30:22.480 --> 01:30:25.165
You're right. You're way too slow.


01:30:26.000 --> 01:30:28.241
Then let me prove you wrong.


01:30:30.800 --> 01:30:33.724
Come on, Mr Kleinschmidt.
do something for your karma.


01:30:34.120 --> 01:30:37.806
He deserves a chance.
- Yes. Let him take the exam.


01:30:42.880 --> 01:30:45.451
AH right. then. Give it a try.


01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:49.286
Thank you.


01:30:49.720 --> 01:30:53.805
Please tell the examiners
not to give me any disability bonus.


01:30:54.240 --> 01:30:56.447
Don't worry, Kahawatte, they won't.


01:30:56.920 --> 01:30:58.410
I'm one of them.


01:31:16.880 --> 01:31:18.609
He's the spoon. she's the fork.


01:31:18.760 --> 01:31:20.569
Yep. spoon always on top.


01:31:31.560 --> 01:31:32.561
Again?
- Yes.


01:31:37.480 --> 01:31:38.447
Keep calm.


01:31:41.480 --> 01:31:42.845
Faster!


01:32:00.920 --> 01:32:03.605
"According to paragraph 30,


01:32:03.840 --> 01:32:07.367
you will be issued
with an extended certificate of conduct.


01:32:08.120 --> 01:32:15.129
You must present this
in order to obtain work as a paramedic."


01:32:16.200 --> 01:32:19.761
So you need to take your passport
to the immigration office.


01:32:23.880 --> 01:32:28.044
"Please sign the attached application..."


01:32:28.200 --> 01:32:30.726
Laura's here.
but she didn't waive this time.


01:32:33.240 --> 01:32:34.401
I'll be right back.


01:32:34.800 --> 01:32:36.404
She's coming over.


01:32:37.440 --> 01:32:39.329
I heard about your speech.


01:32:39.640 --> 01:32:40.402
That's good.


01:32:42.720 --> 01:32:45.087
I'm now officially visually impaired.


01:32:46.400 --> 01:32:48.050
It's not too bad.


01:32:48.680 --> 01:32:51.047
I can actually read instead of pretending.


01:32:52.240 --> 01:32:53.844
And they'll let you take the exam?


01:32:55.040 --> 01:32:56.929
It starts tomorrow morning.


01:32:57.080 --> 01:32:58.923
Drinks and glasses.


01:33:00.280 --> 01:33:03.204
I'll keep my fingers crossed for you.
- Thanks.


01:33:06.800 --> 01:33:08.450
I need to carry on.


01:33:11.000 --> 01:33:14.209
I may be a stupid Afghan,
and things may be different here,


01:33:14.360 --> 01:33:16.647
but if I were you, I'd run after her.


01:33:20.480 --> 01:33:21.891
Watch out. on your right!


01:33:25.280 --> 01:33:26.930
I miss you.


01:33:28.080 --> 01:33:29.081
Take care.


01:33:29.560 --> 01:33:32.370
I miss you,
even if you don't want to hear it.


01:33:42.400 --> 01:33:44.448
Damn pouring loss.


01:34:05.120 --> 01:34:06.804
Take your time, no rush.


01:34:07.320 --> 01:34:08.401
Brandy glass.


01:34:09.280 --> 01:34:10.361
Small whisky tumbler.


01:34:11.920 --> 01:34:13.081
Cocktail glass.


01:34:13.920 --> 01:34:15.763
Acapulco, 480m.


01:34:16.240 --> 01:34:18.607
Champagne glass or flute.


01:34:18.760 --> 01:34:20.649
Tulip glass, 0.2l.


01:34:21.840 --> 01:34:23.285
Caipirinha glass.


01:34:24.160 --> 01:34:25.764
And this is a Martini glass.


01:34:25.960 --> 01:34:28.167
What's a Martini?
- A vermouth.


01:34:28.320 --> 01:34:29.481
What's its origin?


01:34:30.080 --> 01:34:32.447
The slightly bitter Wormwood herb.


01:34:33.040 --> 01:34:35.884
Do you know another Vermouth?
- Cinzano.


01:34:36.120 --> 01:34:37.610
This is the final section.


01:34:37.800 --> 01:34:40.371
When the gong sounds. stop immediately.


01:34:40.640 --> 01:34:42.722
We'll then judge your effort
up to that point.


01:34:42.880 --> 01:34:44.325
Good luck. Your time starts...


01:34:44.520 --> 01:34:45.601
HOW.


01:35:20.160 --> 01:35:21.810
Who's on top again, spoon or fork?


01:35:22.000 --> 01:35:24.606
What's your favourite position
when having sex? - On top.


01:35:24.760 --> 01:35:26.091
You're the spoon.


01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:02.049
One minute left.
You're missing your water glasses. Hurry.


01:36:14.400 --> 01:36:15.890
30 seconds to go.


01:36:42.360 --> 01:36:44.169
No-one touches anything.


01:36:49.720 --> 01:36:53.088
The glasses are not great
but that's a minor thing.


01:37:01.160 --> 01:37:03.640
Not bad. For a youth hostel.


01:37:05.640 --> 01:37:07.483
I'll show you my work of art.


01:37:10.320 --> 01:37:12.482
So. this is the next table.


01:37:16.240 --> 01:37:18.641
Did you do the tie-dye yourself?


01:37:19.280 --> 01:37:21.567
They're rose petals, you fool.


01:37:22.160 --> 01:37:24.925
Mr Kahawatte, to your table, please.


01:37:28.000 --> 01:37:30.287
Now then, Mr Kahawatte, let's see.


01:37:30.440 --> 01:37:33.603
Your table is a disaster,
there's no question about it.


01:37:34.640 --> 01:37:38.247
As a single effort,
this clearly isn't good enough.


01:37:39.600 --> 01:37:43.127
However, since you did well
in your other sections


01:37:43.280 --> 01:37:45.408
and very well in your written exam,


01:37:45.840 --> 01:37:49.447
we've decided,
based on your overall results,


01:37:49.600 --> 01:37:51.170
to award you the diploma.


01:38:08.360 --> 01:38:09.646
Congratulations.


01:38:12.520 --> 01:38:14.921
You were lucky.
- And slightly talented.


01:38:15.840 --> 01:38:19.731
To be honest, I didn't think
you'd last more than a month.


01:38:19.880 --> 01:38:20.961
Neither did I.


01:38:22.320 --> 01:38:24.926
Congratulations.
- Thank you.


01:38:26.160 --> 01:38:29.209
I never doubted that you wanted this
with all your heart.


01:38:29.800 --> 01:38:31.484
Well done.
- Thank you.


01:38:34.200 --> 01:38:35.008
Did you hear that?


01:38:42.640 --> 01:38:45.120
<i>Love you, Sea�.</i>


01:38:45.280 --> 01:38:46.611
Thank you!


01:38:53.520 --> 01:38:56.091
It's unbelievable
how hard they made it for him.


01:38:56.240 --> 01:38:58.322
Does he have a driving Licence?


01:39:00.360 --> 01:39:04.365
I never thought I'd meet anyone
who wants this job more than I do.


01:39:05.440 --> 01:39:09.081
But now I'm not so sure
I haven't already met this person.


01:39:09.240 --> 01:39:10.207
Thank you.


01:39:10.360 --> 01:39:12.408
You have an excellent nose for wine.


01:39:12.640 --> 01:39:14.642
You can work in my restaurant if you like,


01:39:14.800 --> 01:39:16.529
training as a sommelier.


01:39:18.400 --> 01:39:20.289
I'm really honoured.


01:39:21.280 --> 01:39:23.886
But I'm afraid I can't accept your offer.


01:39:25.760 --> 01:39:27.762
Max and I are planning
a venture of our own.


01:39:28.720 --> 01:39:31.405
You keep on surprising me. Kahavvatte.


01:39:32.840 --> 01:39:34.968
Well, then... Good luck.


01:39:37.080 --> 01:39:39.287
You've really earned it.
- Thank you.


01:39:43.120 --> 01:39:44.406
What on earth is he on?


01:40:09.240 --> 01:40:13.370
<i>As the saying goes,
if you want to walk fast, walk alone.</i>


01:40:14.280 --> 01:40:17.602
<i>But if you want to walk far,
walk in good company.</i>


01:40:18.920 --> 01:40:21.446
<i>I was always more of a long-distance guy.</i>


01:40:33.640 --> 01:40:34.766
Do you need a hand?


01:40:40.360 --> 01:40:43.091
I tried to explain to Oskar
why we don't see you anymore.


01:40:43.280 --> 01:40:47.490
He said he lied to me once
because he was afraid I'd stop loving him.


01:40:50.840 --> 01:40:52.524
Looks like you could use some help.


01:40:52.920 --> 01:40:53.967
We really could.


01:40:54.440 --> 01:40:55.248
Great.


01:41:02.160 --> 01:41:05.482
I think Salt's just having
the best moment of his life.


01:41:22.600 --> 01:41:24.443
This is a present from me and Oskar.


01:41:24.600 --> 01:41:25.840
What is it?


01:41:26.000 --> 01:41:27.525
A ball with a bell inside.


01:41:27.680 --> 01:41:31.082
A football for blind people.
Might be more fun this way.


01:41:34.360 --> 01:41:35.441
Come.


01:41:36.360 --> 01:41:38.089
I'll step on everybody's toes.


01:41:39.000 --> 01:41:40.490
I've got two eyes.


01:41:40.880 --> 01:41:42.928
That's plenty for both of us.


01:42:25.560 --> 01:42:30.441
WED LIKE TO THANK SALIYA KAHAWATTE
FOR HIS INSPIRATION AND SUPPORT

